# gpu_hw.cyr — shared by the GPU suites that gate assertions on a context.
#
# Each suite names HW_N, the assertions in its gated section, as counted on an
# AMD host. With no context, gpu_hw_skipped prints that count, so a CI log on a
# runner with no GPU says how much went untested instead of passing quietly.
# With a context, gpu_hw_check asserts the section ran exactly HW_N, so the
# number cannot drift as assertions are added.

fn gpu_hw_skipped(n) {
    print("  SKIPPED: ", 11);
    fmt_int(n);
    println(" hardware assertions (no AMD GPU context on this host)");
    return 0;
}

fn gpu_hw_check(from, n) {
    assert_eq(_assert_total - from, n, "HW_N is the number of hardware assertions that ran");
    return 0;
}

# The NVIDIA suite's skip line. Its gate is a different context constructor, so
# the AMD wording above would misreport which card was missing.
fn gpu_hw_skipped_nvidia(n) {
    print("  SKIPPED: ", 11);
    fmt_int(n);
    println(" hardware assertions (no NVIDIA GPU context on this host)");
    return 0;
}

# The poison word a failed helper fills its stand-in result with. It matches no
# expected value in the GPU suites, its four bytes all differ (so "R equals G"
# style checks fail on it too), and it is not either sentinel (0x5A5A5A5A,
# 0xA5A5A5A5).
var GPU_HW_POISON = 0xDEADBEEF;

# FAIL, DON'T CRASH. A helper that dispatches and reads back used to return 0
# when any step failed, and every caller then read through that 0. On the AMD
# host nothing ever failed, so nothing showed it. On NVIDIA (2.3.2) every
# dispatch failed and two suites segfaulted mid-run, losing every assertion after
# the fault, the count check included.
#
# This records the failure as an assertion named after the step that failed,
# then returns `nbytes` of fresh poison for the caller to read instead. Every
# later check on that result fails on its own line, and the suite runs to its
# summary. The extra failed assertion also moves the HW_N count, so
# gpu_hw_check fails as well, which is correct: the section did not run as
# written.
fn gpu_hw_failed(nbytes, what) {
    assert_eq(0, 1, what);
    var p = fl_alloc(nbytes);
    if (p == 0) { return 0; }
    var i = 0;
    while (i + 4 <= nbytes) { store32(p + i, GPU_HW_POISON); i = i + 4; }
    return p;
}
